        "title": "Reject case-colliding skill package files",
        "body": "Closes #575.\n\nRejects case-colliding skill package files consistently across CLI, web upload, API publish, server publish, and GitHub import discovery. Multipart uploads now reject collisions before blob storage and clean up stored blobs if later payload parsing fails; owned GitHub repo discovery filters colliding tree and code-search candidates before listing them as importable.\n\nProof:\n- Multipart publish with SKILL.md plus skill.md rejects before `storage.store` is called.\n- GitHub owned-repo tree and code-search discovery omit case-colliding candidates.\n- CLI and web publish tests surface the same case-collision error before publish.\n- Local behavior tests passed: `bun run test -- convex/httpApiV1.shared.test.ts convex/lib/githubImport.test.ts convex/githubImport.test.ts packages/schema/src/skillPackageFiles.test.ts src/__tests__/skills-publish-route.test.tsx packages/clawhub/src/cli/commands/publish.test.ts` reported 5 files / 79 tests passing; `bun run format:check` and `bun run ci:types-build` also passed.\n- GitHub Actions on the pushed head have 23 passing non-Vercel checks; the remaining Vercel check is blocked on OpenClaw Foundation team authorization.",
